# Migrate icon reconstruction and platform export to the migration boundary

Preserve the useful cross-platform icon pipeline while replacing only its giant
generated-Rust reconstruction representation. The durable reconstruction plan is
text data owned by `src/migration/icon/`, and local authored/recovered SVGs
remain
ignored evidence rather than distributable repository content.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Keep exact root `Simpsons.ico` mandatory in the lawful source manifest and
  keep `uninst.ico` optional for the game installation.
- [x] Recover the seven SVG assets from the pre-migration authenticated
  transform
  into local `src/migration/icon/assets/` evidence before replacing the old
  representation; keep that directory ignored by Git.
- [x] Make `game/Simpsons.ico` the sole icon reconstruction input. `uninst.ico`
  must not participate in icon authoring, replay, or generated platform output.
- [x] Use the generic Rust function at `src/foundation/algorithm/` to record and
  replay `src/migration/icon/contract/icon_algorithm.txt`; do not generate
  source code as reconstruction data.
- [x] Preserve the useful SVG renderer, platform profiles, and Windows, macOS,
  Linux, Android, and iOS export behavior under `src/migration/icon/` rather
  than deleting it.
- [x] Keep `src/migration/icon/assets/` and `src/migration/icon/out/` ignored;
  never commit the authored/recovered SVGs or generated platform icon products.
- [x] Replay `icon_algorithm.txt` from only lawful `Simpsons.ico` evidence and
  prove all seven local SVG outputs are byte-identical to the recovered oracle.
- [x] Keep `src/unreal/icon/` retired after parity is proven; icon migration and
  export ownership belongs only to `src/migration/icon/`.
- [x] Remove the temporary algorithm reference directory only after generic
  algorithm parity and icon exporter preservation are both complete.

## Evidence

`8c6d8878` established `src/migration/icon/` as the only icon migration
boundary. The tracked `icon_algorithm.txt` is a `shar.algorithm.v1` document
whose single source record is exactly 5,806 bytes with SHA-256
`3b0b72f7b2eff173a81669ee465625e67e70dda8c18282bdeeda6d2a203df328`,
matching `game/Simpsons.ico`. The distinct `game/uninst.ico` identity is absent
from the plan and architecture coverage rejects any plaintext uninstall-icon or
SVG payload marker in the tracked algorithm.

The same commit preserved the SVG renderer, platform profiles, PNG-backed
Windows ICO writer, PNG-backed macOS ICNS writer, Linux hicolor export, Android
adaptive/legacy resources, and iOS AppIcon catalog under the migration function.
`src/migration/icon/assets` and `src/migration/icon/out` are exact Git-ignore
entries; neither local authored/recovered SVG evidence nor generated platform
products is tracked.

A fresh source-bound replay with the current Rust engine reconstructed all seven
ignored SVG targets from only `game/Simpsons.ico`; every byte length and SHA-256
matched `icon_algorithm.txt`. Exporting that recovered tree then produced 58
platform files including Windows `icon.ico`, macOS `icon.icns`, Linux scalable
and raster resources, Android store/resources, and the iOS AppIcon catalog. The
canonical source icon hash was unchanged before and after replay/export.

`src/unreal/icon/` remains retired, and the temporary generic-algorithm
reference
directory was removed only after the reusable exporter had been preserved.
`c7b5eac2` documents the exact local replay/export commands and explicitly
forbids `game/*.ico`, `game/uninst.ico`, or the ignored SVG oracle as substitute
reconstruction evidence.
